on-arrival: e21_after_done = 1

= Levi Was Wrong

Paul Levi had half written a pamphlet against the March Action, sure that it would end in a massacre. It did not, and the pamphlet stays in his drawer. Ruth Fischer tells the Berlin district that the party has learned to fight, and that those who would not fight should step aside.

[? if e21_march_mode = 1 : Levi's friends answer that the strike won because it was a defensive strike of the whole class, which is what Levi always asked for. ?][? if e21_march_mode = 2 : Levi's friends answer that one lucky victory proves nothing, and that next time the Reichswehr will march. ?]

- @admit: Levi admits he was wrong, and stays.
- @warn: Levi goes on warning against adventures.
- @leave: Levi leaves the party.

@admit
subtitle: The party is united, and the Spartacists lose their voice.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 5;
Q.unity += 6;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 5;
!}

Levi writes a short article saying that he underestimated the workers of Central Germany. It is the hardest thing he has ever written. The Left reads it aloud at its meetings.

@warn
subtitle: Levi stays, and the quarrel goes on to the world congress.
on-arrival: e21_levi_fate = 2; offensive_satisfaction -= 8; lean_luxemburgist += 2

Levi publishes an article: a victory won by luck is not a method. The Left demands his expulsion, and the Zentrale sends the question to Moscow.

@leave
subtitle: He goes almost alone. The members, flushed with victory, hardly notice.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 4;
RG.expel('levi', {news: 'Paul Levi returns his membership book', priority: 2});
Q.levi_in_party = 0;
Q.levi_split = 1;
Q.levi_advisor = 0;
if (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') {
    Q.leading_faction = 'unionist';
    Q.junior_faction = 'offensive';
}
Q.unity += 3;
!}

Levi sends his membership book back to the Zentrale with a short letter: the party has chosen a road he cannot follow. A few deputies and journalists go with him.
